description:
Danish Refugee Council, one of the world’s leading humanitarian NGOs, is currently looking for a highly qualified Protection and Peacebuilding Officer for our operations in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia.

Instruction for applicants:
All applicants must upload a cover letter and an updated CV in English. Please ensure that your CV does not exceed three pages. Applications with CVs longer than the specified limit may not be considered


Overall purpose of the role 

Under the line management from Protection Project Manager, technical supervision of CO Protection specialist-Access to justice and HDP Specialist/Coordinator, the protection and Peacebuilding officer will undertake protection, legal aid and multiple Peacebuilding activities within the SIDA Mixed Migration project framework. The officer will be engaged in the provision of legal aid service including legal information dissemination, counselling, assistance, dialogue facilitation and legal representation to the target population. In addition, the officer will take on any additional protection activity as required by the Protection Project Manager to meet the project objective.

Your main duties and responsibilities will be:


	Develop a work plan for the implementation of activities focusing on Legal service provision and Peacebuilding within the framework of the project; 
	Carry out activities focusing on legal support and social cohesion according to work plan and allocated budget in accordance with international and national laws and regulations;   
	Conduct rapid assessment to identify the legal service and social cohesion needs and concern of the target population and frame response according to the identified need; 
	Conduct information dissemination on the legal rights, Civil documentation, and procedures with a focus on issues affecting the target population through the mobile protection desk and community outreach; 
	Provide guidance to protection assistance - key legal information to be shared through the desk; 
	Support advocacy and policy engagement by providing legal analysis, evidence and recommendations on identified legal and policy gaps affecting people on the move, including barriers to safe mobility, access to justice, documentation, return and reintegration, and protection services.
	Provide legal counselling, legal assistance and information dissemination to the target community; 
	Design, coordinate, and facilitate structured dialogue and cultural exchange platforms between migrant and host communities to identify common concerns, strengthen social cohesion, and enhance community-based protection mechanisms
	Develop and deliver capacity-building activities for selected community focal points on mediation, conflict resolution, and dialogue facilitation, and provide ongoing coaching to support sustainable community-led peacebuilding efforts
	Develop and disseminate IEC materials with key messages on legal rights, procedures and available legal and protection services to the target population; 
	Facilitate and advocate access to legal documentation for the target community in collaboration with relevant government authorities and humanitarian agencies;   
	Organize and facilitate capacity-building sessions for government stakeholders, partners and community-based structures on national and international legal frameworks, rights of people on the move, migration-related legal procedures, legal aid and referral mechanisms;
	Engage with DRC finance, administration, supply chain and other relevant teams as required to facilitate timely and compliant implementation of project activities; 
	Conduct regular mapping and updating of legal aid and protection service providers along the Eastern migration route, particularly in Addis Ababa, Dire Dawa, Jigjiga and Togochale, and support the establishment and operationalization of functional referral pathways.
	Support the development, strengthening and operationalization of integrated referral mechanisms for legal aid and protection services in coordination with government institutions, UN agencies, NGOs, legal aid providers and other relevant stakeholders.
	Coordinate with other project teams and implementing partners team.
	Perform other relevant duties and protection activities, as needed or requested by the protection manager.
	Reporting and administrative responsibilities
	Support provision of regular updates on project implementation, including weekly reports, including challenges or barriers to implementation;
	Prepare and submit weekly progress report on legal protection activities to protection manager.
	Ensure that project activities are properly documented and reported 


Experience and technical competencies:


	Minimum 3 years work experience in the legal sector, preferably in a humanitarian context and migration projects;
	Demonstrated experience in providing legal information, legal counselling and legal assistance to vulnerable or marginalized populations
	Experience working with people

